{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b80c-86da-7549-a1f9-c08ebaed1266","session_id":"01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224","message":{"id":"01a1b80c86da7549a1f9c08c7dd29af5","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let's see lib/index.js and lib/commands/models/select.mjs to ensure no breakage. Also check-test-discovery (fixtures dir not included). Also check `lib/commands/models/forecast.mjs` etc. And check the `contracts/spec` for ac-index entries for AC-020..022 to know owners (T-007) and whether traceability will pass.\n\nAlso need to know how `run-tests --ac` filter counts: A-01 expects filtered 3 files for AC-020. Files containing `[AC-020]`: test/unit/select-draft.test.mjs, test/characterization/defects/a5-dup-call.test.mjs, a5-forecast-x3.test.mjs → 3. Good (a5-unused would contain AC-022 only if we tag it as `[AC-022]`... design says a5-unused fixed test title `[fixed] [AC-022] ...` so it's AC-022).\n\nFor AC-021: expected filtered 1 files → only select-draft.test.mjs must contain `[AC-021]`. But wait select-draft.test.mjs contains [AC-020] and [AC-021] tags; filtered by AC-020 → that file is one of 3, fine.\n\nAC-022: filtered 2 files → check-unused.test.mjs and a5-unused.test.mjs.\n\nNote in design 6.4 the traceability files listed for AC-020 include a5-dup-call and a5-forecast-x3 (yes), AC-021 select-draft, AC-022 check-unused + a5-unused.\n\ncheck-traceability expects covered=22 planned=52 after. Currently covered=19 planned=55. Adding 3 covered → 22/52. Good, as long as T-007.json lists exactly these ACs and files exist and one of the files has title containing `[AC-0xx]`.\n\nNow check ac-index for AC-020..022 owners.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":