{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b80f-ab62-7271-93b2-b085b78cb163","session_id":"01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224","message":{"id":"01a1b80fab62727193b2b08350456fb5","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both exit 2 with stderr. Note `echo exit=$?` after shows 2. Good.\n\nNow write test/unit/check-unused.test.mjs (AC-022). Tests:\n\n1. scanPaths on fixtures matches expected items (8).\n2. clean → 0 items.\n3. lib → 0 items.\n4. CLI subprocess: fixture dir exit 1 + --json parse matches; lib exit 0 last stdout line startsWith; unknown arg exit 2.\n5. scanSource unit tests.\n\nRepo root: `fileURLToPath(new URL('../../', import.meta.url))` from test/unit → repo root. Good.\n\nsortKey: file|kind|name.\n\nFor CLI: spawnSync(process.execPath, ['scripts/check-unused.mjs', ...], {cwd: ROOT, encoding:'utf8'}).\n\nTest scanSource cases:\n- comment/string/template-text names don't count:\n```js\nconst src = [\n  \"import { a, b, c, d } from './x.mjs'\",   // but imports of relative path fine\n  \"// a\",\n  \"const s = 'b'\",\n  \"const t = `c`\",\n  \"const u = `${d}`\",\n  \"export { u }\",\n].join('\\n')\n```\nExpected: a, b, c reported (only in comment/string/template text), d not reported (used in `${d}`... but `export { u }`—u defined but not relevant). Wait `const u = \\`${d}\\`` uses d in template expression → counted. So items = a,b,c.\n\nCareful: is `a` in `export { u }`? no.\n\n- `obj.fs` not a reference:\n```js\n\"import fs from 'node:fs'\",\n\"const obj = { fs: 1 }\",\n\"export const value = obj.fs\",\n```\n`obj.fs` — `fs` preceded by '.' → not counted; but object key `{ fs: 1 }` counts as reference per design (\"对象字面量的键 { a: 1 } 无法可靠区分，按引用计\"). So fs would be counted via the key! That breaks the assertion. Use a property access on something else without the key: \n```js\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nconst holder = {}\nexport const value = holder.fs\n```\n`fs` only after '.' → 0 → reported. But `holder` unused variable not reported. Good. items should contain fs (unused). Hmm the design test says \"`obj.fs` 不算引用\" → expect fs reported. Yes.\n\nBetter to make it clearly a positive: assert scanSource(...) deepEqual [{line:1,kind:'import',name:'fs'}].\n\n- regex with quotes doesn't shift scanning:\n```js\n\"import { join } from 'node:path'\",\n\"const re = /[\\\"']/\",\n\"export const value = join('a', 'b')\"\n```\nAssert no items (join counted). Actually line: `const re = /[\"']/` then `join(...)`. If scanner misparsed the regex, it might swallow the next line or count weirdly, possibly reporting join. Assert deepEqual [].\n\n- `export { a as b }` counts `a` as reference:\n```js\n\"import { a } from './x.mjs'\",\n\"export { a as b }\"\n```\nAssert [].\n\n- comments/strings: covered.\n\n- also template nesting? Optional.\n\nAlso could assert scanSource returns line numbers.\n\nLet me write the test file with titles tagged [AC-022].\n\nCareful: this test file itself will be scanned? No — check-unused scans lib only by default. check-unused.test.mjs imports from '../../lib/...'? It imports scanPaths/scanSource from '../../scripts/check-unused.mjs'.\n\nTest 3 (`scanPaths(['lib'])` 0 items) depends on removal of typeOf (task 4). I'll do that later before running tests.\n\nLet me write it.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","_messageId":"01a1b80fab62727193b2b08350456fb5","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b80fab62727193b2b08350456fb5","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b80fab62727193b2b08350456fb5","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b80f-ab62-7271-93b2-b085b78cb163","traceparent":"00-3f40958935830439216b9e572e25ec75-edb4707