{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b80f-eff9-7098-a6cd-6ff8a63ba5b5","session_id":"01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_xFtjzIETE4ShCySGtlj17409","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\007\\lib\\select-draft.mjs"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","_messageId":"01a1b80fd3d37dc9be8a3b71d6a64d10","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b80fd3d37dc9be8a3b71d6a64d10","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b80fd3d37dc9be8a3b71d6a64d10","traceparent":"00-3f40958935830439216b9e572e25ec75-edb47074163b0488-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:10:14.652Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b80f-f00c-787d-8b5e-820e7e50195d","session_id":"01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224","message":{"id":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait: `reason === null || reason === undefined` — reason has default null, so `reason == null` suffices but eslint-free. Fine.\n\nNow rewrite lib/select.mjs.\n\nCareful about the missing-level path: draftSelection with count 0 → truncated false. ok.\n\nAlso should `rejected` in missing-level path be the empty array — yes.\n\nNow the memoization. Write:\n\n```js\nimport { normalizePrices, buildForecast } from './forecast.mjs'\nimport { billedTokens } from './pools.mjs'\nimport { systemNow } from './context.mjs'\nimport { SELECTION_SCHEMA, heavyRejection, draftHandle, draftSelection } from './select-draft.mjs'\n\nexport const SCHEMA = SELECTION_SCHEMA\nexport const LEVELS = [...]\nexport const USAGES = [...]\n```\n\nWait design: \"select.mjs 的 SCHEMA 常量改为从 select-draft.mjs 取值后重导出\" → `export const SCHEMA = SELECTION_SCHEMA`. Good.\n\nFunctions normLevel, normUsage, vendorOf, levelOf, cliCall remain.\n\nusageSamples export:\n\n```js\nexport function usageSamples(records = [], model) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(records)) return []\n  const rows = records.filter((row) => row && row.model === model)\n  return rows.map((row) => {\n    const mtok = billedTokens(row) / 1e6\n    const cost = row.cost_usd\n    return {\n      mtok: Number.isFinite(mtok) && mtok > 0 ? mtok : null,\n      cost_usd: typeof cost === 'number' && Number.isFinite(cost) ? cost : null,\n    }\n  })\n}\n```\n\nDesign says `cost_usd` = row.cost_usd 为有限数则取它，否则 null. `typeof cost === 'number' && Number.isFinite(cost)` is equivalent to Number.isFinite(cost) (Number.isFinite only true for numbers). Use Number.isFinite(cost) ? cost : null.\n\ndefaultForecast:\n\n```js\nfunction buildModelForecast({ model, quota, records, usage, now }) {\n  return buildForecast({ model, quota, samples: usageSamples(records, model), usage, now })\n}\n```\n\nName it something; design says \"默认 forecast 实现（模块内函数，不导出）\". I'll call it `defaultForecast`.\n\nselectModels:\n\n```js\nexport function selectModels(config, request = {}, { status = {}, usage = [], ctx } = {}) {\n  const level = normLevel(request.level || request.tier)\n  const usageKind = normUsage(request.usage)\n  const models = listModels(config, { status, includeDeprecated: true })\n  const count = Math.max(1, Math.min(10, Number(request.count || 1)))\n  const requireVerified = request.require_verified !== false\n  const requireReadonly = request.require_readonly === true\n  const exclude = new Set(request.exclude || [])\n  const allowed = request.candidates ? new Set(request.candidates) : null\n  const rejected = []\n  const records = Array.isArray(usage) ? usage : []\n\n  let clock = null\n  const currentNow = () => {\n    if (clock === null) clock = typeof ctx?.now === 'function' ? ctx.now() : systemNow()\n    return clock\n  }\n  const forecastFn = typeof ctx?.forecast === 'function' ? ctx.forecast : defaultForecast\n  const cache = new Map()\n  const forecastOf = (m) => {\n    const hit = cache.get(m.key)\n    if (hit) return hit\n    const quota = config.quotas?.[m.provider] ?? null\n    const entry = { quota, forecast: forecastFn({ model: m.key, prices: m.prices, quota, records, usage: usageKind, now: currentNow() }) }\n    cache.set(m.key, entry)\n    return entry\n  }\n\n  if (!level) {\n    return draftSelection({ request, level: null, usage: usageKind, models: [], rejected, reason: 'E_LEVEL_REQUIRED', count: 0 })\n  }\n\n  const candidates = models.filter((m) => {\n    if (exclude.has(m.key)) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'excluded' }); return false }\n    if (allowed && !allowed.has(m.key)) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'not_in_workspace_order' }); return false }\n    if (m.level !== level) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: `level:${m.level}` }); return false }\n    if (!m.callable) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: `availability:${m.availability}` }); return false }\n    if (requireVerified && m.identity !== 'verified') { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'identity_unverified' }); return false }\n    if (requireReadonly && !m.readonly) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'readonly_unavailable' }); return false }\n    const refused = heavyRejection({ key: m.key, usage: usageKind, forecast: forecastOf(m).forecast })\n    if (refused) { rejected.push(refused); return false }\n    return true\n  })\n```\n\nWait: `records` — design says \"调用参数是一个对象：{ model, prices, quota, records, usage, now }，其中 ... records 是传入的 usage 数组\". So pass the original `usage` array reference (test asserts same reference). If usage is undefined default [] — the default value is `[]` (new array per call). Test 6.1: \"records（与传入的 usage 数组是同一个引用）\" — for explicit usage array, we pass it. If I do `records = Array.isArray(usage) ? usage : []`, for explicit array it's the same reference. Good.\n\nHmm, if usage is explicitly undefined → `[]` default param, same array used in both? I assign `records = Array.isArray(usage) ? usage : []` → different array literal, but no test cares.\n\nRanking:\n\n```js\n  const rank = (m) => {\n    const f = forecastOf(m).forecast\n    const price = m.prices.input_per_mtok + m.prices.output_per_mtok\n    const unknown = f.risk === 'unknown' ? 1 : 0\n    if (usageKind === 'Heavy') return [unknown, -(f.tasks_left ?? -1), price, m.key]\n    if (usageKind === 'Light') return [price, unknown, m.key]\n    return [unknown, price, m.key]\n  }\n```\n\nunchanged.\n\npicked:\n\n```js\n  const picked = candidates.slice(0, count).map((m) => {\n    const entry = forecastOf(m)\n    return draftHandle({\n      model: m,\n      call: cliCall(config, m, request),\n      forecast: entry.forecast,\n      quota: entry.quota,\n      adapter: config.providers?.[m.provider]?.adapter ?? null,\n    })\n  })\n  return draftSelection({ request, level, usage: usageKind, models: picked, rejected, count })\n```\n\nNote `config.providers[m.provider]?.adapter` in baseline; `config.providers?.[...]` is safer but design says `config.providers[provider]?.adapter ?? null`. Use `config.providers?.[m.provider]?.adapter ?? null`.\n\nCareful: A-02 config has no `adapter` → null.\n\nNow the `forecastOf` quirk: `hit` is an object always truthy. Fine. But what if forecast returns undefined? entry still object.\n\nAlso `Number(request.count || 1)`: keep.\n\nAlso `count` might be NaN if request.count is \"abc\" → Math.max(1, Math.min(10, NaN)) = NaN. Baseline same. Keep.\n\nNow check check-seams: no Date.now, no new Date. `systemNow()` fine. No timers.\n\nPotential check-unused issue: `defaultForecast` used in `forecastFn` ternary. Good. `usageSamples` exported. `billedTokens` used. `normalizePrices` used in listModels. `buildForecast` used in defaultForecast. `systemNow` used.\n\nLet me write the file.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","_messageId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b80f-f00c-787d-8b5e-820e7e50195d","traceparent":"00-3f40958935830439216b9e572e25ec75-edb47074163b0488-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:10:30.456Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b810-2db7-7abe-951c-785ee8bc0f6b","session_id":"01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224","message":{"id":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_gWMPC3Cr6yaQuuHKGxmw6662","name":"Write","input":{"content":"import { normalizePrices, buildForecast } from './forecast.mjs'\nimport { billedTokens } from './pools.mjs'\nimport { systemNow } from './context.mjs'\nimport { SELECTION_SCHEMA, heavyRejection, draftHandle, draftSelection } from './select-draft.mjs'\n\nexport const SCHEMA = SELECTION_SCHEMA\nexport const LEVELS = ['Top', 'High', 'Middle', 'Quick']\nexport const USAGES = ['Heavy', 'Normal', 'Light']\n\nfunction normLevel(v) {\n  const s = String(v || '').trim().toLowerCase()\n  return LEVELS.find((x) => x.toLowerCase() === s) || null\n}\nfunction normUsage(v) {\n  const s = String(v || '').trim().toLowerCase()\n  return USAGES.find((x) => x.toLowerCase() === s) || 'Normal'\n}\n\nfunction vendorOf(provider) {\n  const p = String(provider || '').toLowerCase()\n  if (p.includes('claude')) return 'anthropic'\n  if (p.includes('codex') || p.includes('openai')) return 'openai'\n  if (p.includes('codebuddy') || p.includes('tencent')) return 'tencent'\n  if (p.includes('cursor') || p.includes('xai') || p.includes('grok')) return 'xai'\n  if (p.includes('gemini') || p.includes('google')) return 'google'\n  return p\n}\n\nfunction levelOf(m) {\n  if (m.level && LEVELS.includes(m.level)) return m.level\n  if (m.tier === 'top') return 'Top'\n  if (m.tier === 'advanced') return 'High'\n  if (m.tier === 'standard') return 'Middle'\n  return 'Quick'\n}\n\nfunction cliCall(config, model, request) {\n  const p = config.providers?.[model.provider] || {}\n  const id = model.id\n  const cwd = request.cwd || '<workspace>'\n  if (model.provider === 'claude') {\n    return { command: p.cli, args: ['-p', '--model', id, '--output-format', 'stream-json', '--verbose'], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n  }\n  if (model.provider === 'codex') {\n    return { command: p.cli, args: ['exec', '--model', id, '-s', 'read-only', '--skip-git-repo-check', '--json'], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n  }\n  if (model.provider === 'codebuddy') {\n    return { command: p.cli, args: ['-p', '--model', id, '--output-format', 'stream-json', '--verbose'], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n  }\n  if (model.provider === 'cursor-wsl') {\n    return { command: p.cli, args: ['-e', 'bash', '-lc', `cd '${cwd}' && agent -p --force --model '${id}'`], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n  }\n  if (model.provider === 'gemini') {\n    return { command: p.cli, args: ['-m', id, '-p'], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n  }\n  return { command: p.cli || null, args: [], input: 'stdin', cwd }\n}\n\n/** Usage ledger rows of one model projected to the forecast sample shape. */\nexport function usageSamples(records = [], model) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(records)) return []\n  return records\n    .filter((row) => row && row.model === model)\n    .map((row) => {\n      const mtok = billedTokens(row) / 1e6\n      return {\n        mtok: Number.isFinite(mtok) && mtok > 0 ? mtok : null,\n        cost_usd: Number.isFinite(row.cost_usd) ? row.cost_usd : null,\n      }\n    })\n}\n\nfunction defaultForecast({ model, quota, records, usage, now }) {\n  return buildForecast({ model, quota, samples: usageSamples(records, model), usage, now })\n}\n\nexport function listModels(config, { status = {}, includeDeprecated = false } = {}) {\n  return Object.entries(config.models).map(([key, m]) => {\n    const st = status[m.provider] || { state: 'unavailable', detail: 'provider not checked' }\n    const callable = st.state === 'callable' && !m.deprecated\n    return {\n      schema: 'cliworker.model/v1', key, provider: m.provider, id: m.id || key,\n      vendor: m.vendor || vendorOf(m.provider), tier: m.tier || 'unknown', level: levelOf(m),\n      identity: m.identity === 'verified' ? 'verified' : 'unverified',\n      identity_group: m.identity_group || null,\n      deprecated: !!m.deprecated, deprecated_reason: m.deprecated_reason || null,\n      callable, availability: callable ? 'callable' : (m.deprecated ? 'deprecated' : st.state),\n      readonly: m.readonly === undefined ? !!(config.providers?.[m.provider]?.readonly) : !!m.readonly,\n      prices: normalizePrices(m), source: 'config',\n      provider_detail: st.detail || null,\n    }\n  }).filter((m) => includeDeprecated || !m.deprecated)\n}\n\nexport function selectModels(config, request = {}, { status = {}, usage = [], ctx } = {}) {\n  const level = normLevel(request.level || request.tier)\n  const usageKind = normUsage(request.usage)\n  const models = listModels(config, { status, includeDeprecated: true })\n  const count = Math.max(1, Math.min(10, Number(request.count || 1)))\n  const requireVerified = request.require_verified !== false\n  const requireReadonly = request.require_readonly === true\n  const exclude = new Set(request.exclude || [])\n  const allowed = request.candidates ? new Set(request.candidates) : null\n  const rejected = []\n  const records = Array.isArray(usage) ? usage : []\n\n  let clock = null\n  const currentNow = () => {\n    if (clock === null) clock = typeof ctx?.now === 'function' ? ctx.now() : systemNow()\n    return clock\n  }\n  const forecastFn = typeof ctx?.forecast === 'function' ? ctx.forecast : defaultForecast\n  const cache = new Map()\n  // One quota read and one forecast call per model that clears the pre-filter, cached by key:\n  // ranking and handle building only ever see the cached entry.\n  const forecastOf = (m) => {\n    const hit = cache.get(m.key)\n    if (hit) return hit\n    const quota = config.quotas?.[m.provider] ?? null\n    const entry = {\n      quota,\n      forecast: forecastFn({ model: m.key, prices: m.prices, quota, records, usage: usageKind, now: currentNow() }),\n    }\n    cache.set(m.key, entry)\n    return entry\n  }\n\n  if (!level) {\n    return draftSelection({ request, level: null, usage: usageKind, models: [], rejected, reason: 'E_LEVEL_REQUIRED', count: 0 })\n  }\n\n  const candidates = models.filter((m) => {\n    if (exclude.has(m.key)) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'excluded' }); return false }\n    if (allowed && !allowed.has(m.key)) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'not_in_workspace_order' }); return false }\n    if (m.level !== level) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: `level:${m.level}` }); return false }\n    if (!m.callable) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: `availability:${m.availability}` }); return false }\n    if (requireVerified && m.identity !== 'verified') { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'identity_unverified' }); return false }\n    if (requireReadonly && !m.readonly) { rejected.push({ key: m.key, reason: 'readonly_unavailable' }); return false }\n    const refused = heavyRejection({ key: m.key, usage: usageKind, forecast: forecastOf(m).forecast })\n    if (refused) { rejected.push(refused); return false }\n    return true\n  })\n\n  const rank = (m) => {\n    const f = forecastOf(m).forecast\n    const price = m.prices.input_per_mtok + m.prices.output_per_mtok\n    const unknown = f.risk === 'unknown' ? 1 : 0\n    if (usageKind === 'Heavy') return [unknown, -(f.tasks_left ?? -1), price, m.key]\n    if (usageKind === 'Light') return [price, unknown, m.key]\n    return [unknown, price, m.key]\n  }\n  candidates.sort((a, b) => {\n    const ra = rank(a), rb = rank(b)\n    for (let i = 0; i < ra.length; i++) { if (ra[i] < rb[i]) return -1; if (ra[i] > rb[i]) return 1 }\n    return 0\n  })\n\n  const picked = candidates.slice(0, count).map((m) => {\n    const entry = forecastOf(m)\n    return draftHandle({\n      model: m,\n      call: cliCall(config, m, request),\n      forecast: entry.forecast,\n      quota: entry.quota,\n      adapter: config.providers?.[m.provider]?.adapter ?? null,\n    })\n  })\n  return draftSelection({ request, level, usage: usageKind, models: picked, rejected, count })\n}\n","file_path":"C:/git/dsh-CLIWorker/.collab/worktrees/007/lib/select.mjs"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":135728,"output_tokens":4087,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":135552,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","_messageId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b80ff00c787d8b5e820c2133014d","traceparent":"00-3f40958935830439216b9e572e25ec75-edb47074163b0488-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b80c-10a1-714c-94fe-186218e3e224,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b80c14647279947af18522731dd8"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:10:30.456Z"}
